net: Allow an empty SOCKS5 password

RFC 1929 gives the password field 1 to 255 bytes, so the SOCKS5
username/password patch refused an empty one. Some proxies are set up
with a username and no password, and other clients (libcurl among them)
log in to them with a zero-length password field. The embedder decides
whether to offer such a login; the socket only has to send it.

Accept an empty password and send it as PLEN 0. The username must still
be 1 to 255 bytes long.

diff --git a/net/socket/socks5_client_socket.cc b/net/socket/socks5_client_socket.cc
--- a/net/socket/socks5_client_socket.cc
+++ b/net/socket/socks5_client_socket.cc
@@ -392,7 +392,7 @@
 int SOCKS5ClientSocket::DoAuthWrite() {
   if (!write_buf_) {
     const auto& [username, password] = *credentials_;
-    if (username.empty() || username.size() > 0xFF || password.empty() ||
+    if (username.empty() || username.size() > 0xFF ||
         password.size() > 0xFF) {
       return ERR_SOCKS_CONNECTION_FAILED;
     }
diff --git a/net/socket/socks5_client_socket.h b/net/socket/socks5_client_socket.h
--- a/net/socket/socks5_client_socket.h
+++ b/net/socket/socks5_client_socket.h
@@ -60,7 +60,9 @@
                                      std::string* password);
   static void SetCredentialsLookup(CredentialsLookup lookup);
   // Offers username/password authentication besides none, and uses it if
-  // the proxy picks it. Each must be 1 to 255 bytes long.
+  // the proxy picks it. The username must be 1 to 255 bytes long, the
+  // password at most 255 (crnet: an empty one goes out as PLEN 0, as
+  // other clients send it, for proxies set up without a password).
   void SetCredentials(std::string username, std::string password);
   // Called by SOCKSConnectJob with the proxy this socket is connected to.
   void LookUpCredentials(const HostPortPair& proxy,
